Z||000011||HugGRRRFiero||08-14-2000||12:31 AM||||mbramble,<P>   If your open to an alternative to Mecham or IRM scoops, BBJ Resin Specialties is offering a little more affordable custom scoop that bolts into the stock side air vent opening.  It's easy to bolt-on with no modifications.  I've got one on my Fiero and grabs attention anywhere I go.<P>If you'd like to check them out here's the link:<BR><A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bbjproducts" TARGET=_blank>BBJ Resin Specialties</A><P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||mrfiero||08-14-2000||12:40 AM||||The side scoops were a design study by GM and they scrapped the idea after discovering that they were prone to chipping. <P>No Fiero came with these scoops from the factory, which is too bad because I think they look better (I really like the Mecham style ones).<P>  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 08-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||ur2biteme||08-14-2000||03:34 AM||||i think you're just a shade over my height darklord, i'm just a little over 6'1".  it seems as though they designed these cars for people that are all leg and no torso  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  this is the only car that i've owned that i havent had to set the seat as far back as it could go, and in the case of my '94 mustang, i had to recline the seat too!  headroom seems to be the problem here.  <P>Back to the topic:  The fiero store sells some similar to the ones monkeyman has posted, but i think they are knockoffs, dont know how much they are.  i was gonna call about them myself.  if i'm not lazy after work tomorrow, i'll call and find out before i go over to big-o's shop.  gonna find out what the total is gonna be for my suspension<BR>rebuild. i'm kinda fearing the worst  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
