Z||000017||Dan86gt3.8||08-14-2000||04:00 PM||||supposedly fooca sells them.   I am also looking for the mecham stylke with the strakes.  I wanted some before I painted but its too late for that.  Also, I want to know what kind of quality you guys got them.  I talked to a guy here in town that has them and he said he had to work on them for a couple weeks to get them smooth and also that they did not fit right and he had to twist or bend them to get them on.  Plus I don't even think pisa or fiero store sells them anymore.  And about thoose canadian ones, has anyone on the board have them?  If you order from the us do you have to get canadian money or how does that work (don't mena to offend any canadians here I have just never ordered anything from outside the us)  Also is the quality of the canadian scoops pretty good or at lkeast do they fit?  As long as they fit they would be fine in my book because you can eventually make anything smooth but it aloitt harder to MAKE them fit the car.||||reg||1
Z||000018||sloGT||08-14-2000||04:15 PM||||Dan86,Pisa still sells them.I got mine from them,and you do have a lot of fitting,bending,beating,slinging and cursing.The bottoms would not line up at all and had to be cut and reformed.oh well maybe it's just me,maybe it's pisa.But I wont even start on thier euro fascia.I finally got it to fit after a month and a half.||||reg||13
Z||000019||contra||08-14-2000||05:56 PM||||about the question from the canadian fiero shop (www.thefieroshop.com)...<BR>i buy from them all the time. i got my scoops for around $225 or so for the pair. They were very good quality, already smoothed, and had a nice white gelcoat on them. They didn't however cut any holes or anything in them for the GFX and molding clips, but they have the spots marked off clearly. It took me a total of 5hours to put them on my car, and i'm still an amateur!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I didn't have to bend or twist at all, just a little cutting. ||||reg||1
